      "title": "El Niño-linked floods force Southwest evacuations; Arizona declares emergency",
      "content_html": "Pacific storm systems brought torrential rain and flooding across the normally arid Southwest, prompting evacuations in Arizona, Colorado, New Mexico and Utah. The National Weather Service said El Niño was disrupting weather patterns as the region faced another round of heavy rain. Arizona Gov. Katie Hobbs declared a statewide emergency Monday to help local authorities clear roads, repair infrastructure and assist displaced residents. At least one person died in the flooding; police said a second death in Flagstaff appeared weather-related, pending an official determination.\n\nFormer National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration chief scientist Ryan Maue estimated that more than 20 trillion gallons of water fell across the Four Corners states and Nevada over two weeks. Flooding damaged roads and bridges, stranded residents and caused sewage to back up into some homes. Although rain had ended in parts of the Southwest by Monday, flooding along some swollen waterways could continue through at least Tuesday.",
