      "url": "https://cincodias.elpais.com/mercados-financieros/2026-11-03/wall-street-afronta-las-midterms-mas-riesgo-regulatorio-para-la-ia-y-alivio-pasajero-para-la-deuda.html",
      "title": "US midterms put AI oversight and data center permits in focus",
      "content_html": "Voters in the U.S. midterm elections on Nov. 3 will determine control of Congress and choose governors in 36 states. The contests could shape scrutiny of artificial intelligence companies and permitting for data centers. Wall Street forecasts point to a Democratic House, while Senate control remains uncertain. Whichever party wins, President Donald Trump retains his veto, limiting the prospect of sweeping federal legislation.\n\nDemocratic gains could bring congressional investigations into AI firms and proposals for model safety testing, incident reporting and greater accountability for data center developers. Analysts expect state and local decisions on power, water, land use and construction permits to affect projects more directly. One bank analysis estimated that even heightened scrutiny would reach only about 15% of U.S. data center capacity, leaving the overall investment cycle largely intact. Congress is scheduled to reconvene on Nov. 9, with federal funding negotiations due before a Dec. 11 deadline.",
